# countLeadingZeroes

- _countLeadingZeroes(n, b=2, w=32)_

Answer the number of leading zero bits in the _w_-bit base-_b_ representation of the number _n_.

```
>>> 1.countLeadingZeroes(2, 32)
31

>>> 1.countLeadingZeroes(2, 64)
63

>>> 4.countLeadingZeroes(2, 32)
29

>>> 1000.countLeadingZeroes(2, 32)
22
```

* * *

See also: integerDigits

Guides: Bitwise Functions, Integer Functions
